Here is a script that generates glowing text with an animated rainbow gradient border using HTML and CSS. This approach uses a wrapper element for the border and an inner element for the text, which is a common and well-supported technique.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Glowing Text with Animated Border</title>
    <style>
        /* Basic setup for centering and background */
        body {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            background: #101010;
            margin: 0;
            font-family: sans-serif;
        }

        /* The wrapper div creates the border effect */
        .border-wrapper {
            position: relative;
            padding: 4px; /* This controls the border thickness */
            border-radius: 20px;
            /* A multi-color gradient for the rainbow effect */
            background: linear-gradient(60deg, #f79533, #f37055, #ef4e7b, #a166ab, #5073b8, #1098ad, #07b39b, #6fba82);
            /* Make the gradient larger than the element to allow for animation */
            background-size: 300% 300%;
            animation: animated-gradient 4s ease-in-out infinite;
        }

        /* The keyframe animation for the gradient background */
        @keyframes animated-gradient {
            0% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
            50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }
            100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
        }

        /* The main text element */
        .glowing-text {
            background: #101010; /* Match the body background to hide the wrapper's center */
            color: #fff;
            padding: 2rem 4rem;
            border-radius: 16px; /* Slightly smaller than the wrapper's border-radius */
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
