}
```

You would then add this single filter to your `SecurityFilterChain`. This approach is less flexible because the entire filter chain structure remains the same; only the logic at this one point changes. The multiple `SecurityFilterChain` approach is superior as it allows for completely different configurations (e.g., different authentication methods, CSRF settings, etc.) for each case.

